        <p>To close, the idea is simple. Most systems react to the world after it moves. We run the world forward first, inside a living, checkable simulation, and let people place predictions on what comes next. The game is the skin; the moat is the combination of a checkable world, promise-constrained generation, and a living society, and the business is a two-track model with a self-policing prediction market. We would be glad to walk you through a live world and answer questions. Thank you.</p>
